@@ -255,6 +255,7 @@ Bugs
 - Document why :class:`moabb.datasets.BNCI2015_003` subjects 1 and 2 have a 1:35 ``Target``/``NonTarget`` ratio (150 / 5250 epochs) instead of the 1:5 of subjects 3-10 (300 / 1500): ``s1.mat`` and ``s2.mat`` were recorded with the single-character speller (36 flash codes, one target), the others with the row/column speller (12 flash codes, two targets). The loader returns every flash in the released files; the counts come from the data, not from event decoding (:gh:`274` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Rozado2015` returning a trigger channel as ``Fp1`` and EEG 32 times too small. Channel 0 of the 57-channel BioSemi XDF stream is ``Trig1``, but the loader took the first 32 channels by position, so ``Fp1`` held the trigger code, every other label was shifted by one electrode and ``Cz`` was dropped; it also scaled the stream's microvolt values as raw ADC counts (31.25 nV) instead of 1e-6. The scalp channels are now picked by their stream label and scaled from the declared microvolts; the median absolute 8-30 Hz epoch amplitude goes from 0.11 uV to 3.5 uV (median over the 30 subjects); the docstring also flags the two noisy subjects (10, 15) and the two 75-trial subjects (16, 18) (:gh:`1070` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Rozado2015` returning a trigger channel as ``Fp1`` and EEG 32 times too small. Channel 0 of the 57-channel BioSemi XDF stream is ``Trig1``, but the loader took the first 32 channels by position, so ``Fp1`` held the trigger code, every other label was shifted by one electrode and ``Cz`` was dropped; it also scaled the stream's microvolt values as raw ADC counts (31.25 nV) instead of 1e-6. The scalp channels are now picked by their stream label and scaled from the declared microvolts; the median absolute 8-30 Hz epoch amplitude goes from 0.11 uV to 3.5 uV (median over the 30 subjects); the docstring also flags the two noisy subjects (10, 15) and the two 75-trial subjects (16, 18). Delete cached epochs and results computed before this fix and re-run (:gh:`1070` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
+- Fix the log record :class:`moabb.datasets.EPFLP300` writes when it unzips a subject archive: ``logger.info("unzip", path_zip)`` passed the path without a ``%s`` placeholder, so formatting the record raised ``TypeError: not all arguments converted during string formatting``. Stock handlers only print that error, but any handler that formats records strictly, such as one that re-raises formatting errors, made ``get_data`` fail (:gh:`1298` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 
